          {
            "label": "Back-fill without doubles",
            "sections": [
              {
                "heading": "Back-fill without doubles",
                "accent": "blue",
                "text": [
                  "An independent incident from Flow 2 — a shorter (47-minute) outage at the same site that never fills the ring, shown to teach the dedup path.",
                  "The buffer back-fills after reconnect, with dedup and timeline reconciliation, so the household sees one honest timeline and one summary notification instead of a burst of stale alerts."
                ],
                "bullets": [
                  "The access point returns; Warden reassociates and resumes its TLS session, and Skybridge resyncs the clock and returns the last event_uid it has acked.",
                  "Warden sends Timeline a back-fill manifest listing four buffered events with timestamps, durations, and clip hashes.",
                  "Timeline dedups the manifest against its index and returns the upload list — `ev-4410` was uploaded just before the drop but never acked, so it is marked duplicate and skipped.",
                  "Warden uploads the three missing clips oldest-first to Inlet at background priority so live traffic always wins.",
                  "Inlet writes each clip to Coldstore and acks each event_uid, and Warden flips each acked flash segment to reclaimable.",
                  "Timeline splices the back-filled events in at their recorded timestamps and badges the outage window \"recovered offline\".",
                  "Timeline sends the batch to Scribe, which captions all three in one call, and attaches the captions without re-notifying per event.",
                  "Courier pushes a single summary — \"Warden was offline 47 min; 3 events recovered\" — instead of three stale alerts.",
                  "**Inlet down** — the same flash buffer absorbs it: unacked events stay buffered and the back-fill flow runs on recovery, so a cloud ingest outage looks like a wifi outage to the camera.",
                  "**Timeline down** — acks stop, so segments stay protected until acked: no data loss, just delayed dedup and splice."
                ],
                "contract": {
                  "title": "On the wire: back-fill manifest (Warden → Timeline)",
                  "source": "https://github.com/nestrel/firmware/blob/main/warden/buffer/flashring.c#L77",
                  "fields": [
                    {"k": "cam_id", "v": "\"warden-7f9\"", "g": "device identity"},
                    {"k": "outage_start", "v": "1757088120", "g": "when the uplink dropped"},
                    {"k": "outage_end", "v": "1757090940", "g": "when the TLS session resumed"},
                    {"k": "clock_skew_ms", "v": "1840", "g": "correction Skybridge applied; Timeline shifts timestamps"},
                    {"k": "events", "v": "[{\"uid\":\"ev-4410\",\"ts\":1757088180,\"dur_s\":19,\"sha256\":\"9c41…\"},…]", "g": "one entry per buffered event; uid is the dedup key", "hot": true},
                    {"k": "dropped", "v": "0", "g": "events lost to ring overwrite during the outage"}
                  ],
                  "note": "Sent in Flow 3 step 2, right after the access point returns."
                },
                "diagram": {
                  "groups": {"warden": {"title": "Warden camera"}},
                  "nodes": {
                    "conn": {"title": "Conn manager", "sub": "wifi + tls", "icon": "antenna", "tint": "dev", "group": "warden"},
                    "flash": {"title": "Flash buffer", "sub": "4 events held", "icon": "db", "tint": "dev", "group": "warden"},
                    "skybridge": {"title": "Skybridge", "sub": "device gateway", "icon": "cloud", "tint": "cmd",
                      "link": "https://github.com/nestrel/cloud/blob/main/services/skybridge/session.go#L86"},
                    "timeline": {"title": "Timeline", "sub": "dedup + splice", "icon": "db", "tint": "data",
                      "link": "https://github.com/nestrel/cloud/blob/main/services/timeline/reconcile.go#L133"},
                    "inlet": {"title": "Inlet", "sub": "media ingest", "icon": "server", "tint": "cmd",
                      "link": "https://github.com/nestrel/cloud/blob/main/services/inlet/ingest.go#L131"},
                    "coldstore": {"title": "Coldstore", "sub": "object store", "icon": "db", "tint": "data",
                      "link": "https://github.com/nestrel/cloud/blob/main/services/coldstore/objects.go#L58"},
                    "scribe": {"title": "Scribe", "sub": "LLM captioner", "icon": "server", "tint": "cmd",
                      "link": "https://github.com/nestrel/cloud/blob/main/services/scribe/describe.go#L49"},
                    "courier": {"title": "Courier", "sub": "notifications", "icon": "cloud", "tint": "cmd",
                      "link": "https://github.com/nestrel/cloud/blob/main/services/courier/push.go#L72"},
                    "phone": {"title": "Household", "sub": "nestrel app", "icon": "phone", "tint": "dev"}
                  },
                  "rows": [
                    [["conn", "flash"], "skybridge", "timeline"],
                    ["inlet", "coldstore", "scribe"]
                  ],
                  "floats": [
                    {"id": "courier", "side": "below"},
                    {"id": "phone", "side": "below"}
                  ],
                  "edges": [
                    {"from": "conn", "to": "skybridge", "kind": "https", "label": "TLS resume"},
                    {"from": "skybridge", "to": "conn", "kind": "https", "ret": true, "label": "clock+last uid"},
                    {"from": "conn", "to": "timeline", "kind": "https", "label": "manifest 4 ev"},
                    {"from": "timeline", "to": "conn", "kind": "https", "ret": true, "label": "upload list 3"},
                    {"from": "conn", "to": "inlet", "kind": "https", "label": "clips bg-prio"},
                    {"from": "inlet", "to": "coldstore", "kind": "int", "label": "write object"},
                    {"from": "inlet", "to": "conn", "kind": "https", "ret": true, "label": "ack ev_uid"},
                    {"from": "timeline", "to": "scribe", "kind": "int", "label": "batch describe"},
                    {"from": "scribe", "to": "timeline", "kind": "int", "ret": true, "label": "3 captions"},
                    {"from": "timeline", "to": "courier", "kind": "int", "label": "1 summary"},
                    {"from": "courier", "to": "phone", "kind": "https", "label": "summary push"}
                  ],
                  "panels": [
                    {"id": "sig", "type": "signal", "title": "Uplinks",
                      "links": [
                        {"id": "wifi", "label": "Wi-Fi", "transport": "wifi"},
                        {"id": "cloud", "label": "Cloud session", "transport": "wifi"}
                      ],
                      "initial": {"wifi": {"state": "lost"}, "cloud": {"state": "lost"}}},
                    {"id": "buf", "type": "buffer", "title": "Flash event buffer", "capacity": "60 min", "segments": 12,
                      "initial": {"head": 4, "cells": ["buffered", "buffered", "buffered", "buffered"]}},
                    {"id": "rlog", "type": "log", "title": "Reconciliation", "tags": {"NET": "#4ADE80", "IDX": "#FBBF24", "LLM": "#A78BFA"}}
                  ],
                  "steps": [
                    {"edges": ["conn->skybridge", "skybridge->conn"], "text": "AP back — TLS resumed, clock resynced",
                      "panels": {"sig": {"wifi": {"state": "ok"}, "cloud": {"state": "ok"}}, "rlog": {"log": [{"tag": "NET", "text": "skew +1.8 s corrected"}]}}},
                    {"edge": "conn->timeline", "text": "Manifest of 4 buffered events sent",
                      "panels": {"rlog": {"log": [{"tag": "NET", "text": "manifest: 4 buffered events"}]}}},
                    {"edge": "timeline->conn", "text": "Dedup: ev-4410 already indexed — skipped",
                      "panels": {"rlog": {"log": [{"tag": "IDX", "text": "ev-4410 duplicate — skip"}]}, "buf": {"mark": [[0, 0, "uploaded"]], "note": "ev-4410 duplicate — reclaimable"}}},
                    {"edge": "conn->inlet", "text": "Oldest-first upload at background priority",
                      "panels": {"buf": {"mark": [[1, 1, "uploading"]], "note": "uploading oldest missing clip"}}},
                    {"edges": ["inlet->coldstore", "inlet->conn"], "text": "Each ack flips a segment reclaimable",
                      "panels": {"buf": {"mark": [[1, 1, "uploaded"], [2, 2, "uploading"]], "note": "one clip acked — uploading next"}}},
                    {"nodes": ["timeline"], "text": "Events spliced at recorded timestamps; gap badged",
                      "panels": {"rlog": {"log": [{"tag": "IDX", "text": "47 min gap badged"}]}, "buf": {"mark": [[2, 2, "uploaded"], [3, 3, "uploaded"]], "note": "remaining clips acked"}}},
                    {"edges": ["timeline->scribe", "scribe->timeline"], "text": "Batch captions — no per-event re-notify",
                      "panels": {"rlog": {"log": [{"tag": "LLM", "text": "3 captions attached"}]}}},
                    {"edges": ["timeline->courier", "courier->phone"], "text": "One summary push: offline 47 min, 3 recovered",
                      "panels": {"rlog": {"log": [{"tag": "NET", "text": "summary sent — not 3 alerts"}]}}}
                  ]
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "label": "Overnight wave, with a parachute",
            "sections": [
              {
                "heading": "Overnight wave, with a parachute",
                "accent": "violet",
                "text": [
                  "The staged overnight firmware rollout ships with health-checked automatic rollback."
                ],
                "bullets": [
                  "A release engineer promotes firmware 4.2.0 in Foundry, which opens wave 3 (5% of the fleet) for the overnight window.",
                  "Foundry queries Vitals for each wave-3 camera's health and skips any that is offline, mid-event, or running hot.",
                  "Foundry publishes the update offer to Skybridge, which delivers it to Warden's control channel at 02:10 local.",
                  "Warden confirms it is idle — no live view, no buffered backlog — and downloads the signed image from Foundry's artifact store.",
                  "Warden verifies the signature and digest against its secure-boot keys, writes the image to slot B marked boot-once, and reboots — recording pauses about 40 seconds.",
                  "The new firmware starts its health check: camera pipeline up, buffer partition mounted, TLS session established within 120 seconds.",
                  "The 4.2.0 wifi driver fails to associate inside the window, so the boot watchdog reboots the camera into slot A automatically — no cloud round-trip needed.",
                  "Slot A (4.1.7) comes back, reconnects, and reports the rollback with failure code `WIFI_ASSOC_TIMEOUT` to Vitals.",
                  "Vitals feeds wave statistics to Foundry, which holds wave 3 when rollbacks cross 1% and pages the release engineer.",
                  "**Firmware update fails** — slot B never becomes default until the health check passes; boot-once plus the watchdog guarantees an unattended return to slot A."
                ],
                "contract": {
                  "title": "On the wire: update offer (Foundry → Warden via Skybridge)",
                  "source": "https://github.com/nestrel/firmware/blob/main/warden/ota/slots.c#L164",
                  "fields": [
                    {"k": "release_id", "v": "\"rel-420-w3\"", "g": "release + wave identity for telemetry"},
                    {"k": "version", "v": "\"4.2.0\"", "g": "target firmware version"},
                    {"k": "image_url", "v": "\"https://fw.nestrel.io/warden/4.2.0.img\"", "g": "artifact-store download"},
                    {"k": "sha256", "v": "\"e07b…\"", "g": "image digest, checked before flashing"},
                    {"k": "sig", "v": "\"b64:MEUC…\"", "g": "release signature, checked against secure-boot keys", "hot": true},
                    {"k": "window", "v": "\"01:00-05:00\"", "g": "local install window; offer expires outside it"},
                    {"k": "health_timeout_s", "v": "120", "g": "how long the post-boot health check may take", "hot": true}
                  ],
                  "note": "Sent in Flow 4 step 3, when the offer lands on Warden's control channel at 02:10 local."
                },
                "diagram": {
                  "nodes": {
                    "eng": {"title": "Release eng", "sub": "foundry console", "icon": "terminal", "tint": "cmd"},
                    "foundry": {"title": "Foundry", "sub": "wave coordinator", "icon": "server", "tint": "cmd",
                      "link": "https://github.com/nestrel/cloud/blob/main/services/foundry/waves.go#L212"},
                    "artifacts": {"title": "Artifact store", "sub": "signed images", "icon": "db", "tint": "data"},
                    "vitals": {"title": "Vitals", "sub": "fleet health", "icon": "db", "tint": "data",
                      "link": "https://github.com/nestrel/cloud/blob/main/services/vitals/health.go#L94"},
                    "skybridge": {"title": "Skybridge", "sub": "device gateway", "icon": "cloud", "tint": "cmd",
                      "link": "https://github.com/nestrel/cloud/blob/main/services/skybridge/session.go#L86"},
                    "warden": {"title": "Warden", "sub": "slot A 4.1.7", "icon": "chip", "tint": "dev"}
                  },
                  "rows": [
                    ["eng", "foundry", "artifacts"],
                    ["vitals", "skybridge", "warden"]
                  ],
                  "edges": [
                    {"from": "eng", "to": "foundry", "kind": "https", "label": "promote 4.2.0"},
                    {"from": "foundry", "to": "vitals", "kind": "int", "label": "health query"},
                    {"from": "foundry", "to": "skybridge", "kind": "int", "label": "wave 3 offers"},
                    {"from": "skybridge", "to": "warden", "kind": "mqtt", "label": "UPDATE offer"},
                    {"from": "warden", "to": "artifacts", "kind": "https", "label": "GET image"},
                    {"from": "warden", "to": "skybridge", "kind": "mqtt", "label": "rollback evt"},
                    {"from": "skybridge", "to": "vitals", "kind": "int", "label": "record fail"},
                    {"from": "vitals", "to": "foundry", "kind": "int", "label": "wave stats"},
                    {"from": "foundry", "to": "eng", "kind": "https", "label": "page on-call"}
                  ],
                  "panels": [
                    {"id": "slot", "type": "state", "title": "Firmware slots",
                      "states": ["RUN_A", "OFFERED", "DOWNLOAD", "FLASH_B", "HEALTH", "ROLLBACK"],
                      "colors": {"ROLLBACK": "#F87171", "RUN_A": "#4ADE80"},
                      "initial": {"state": "RUN_A"}},
                    {"id": "flog", "type": "log", "title": "OTA log", "tags": {"SYS": "#94A3B8", "OTA": "#FBBF24"}}
                  ],
